      "The Amazon listing has only three bullets and names a parts dealer as its brand",
      "Spirit’s page recommends a 20-amp circuit; the owner’s manual we found says 15-amp dedicated",
      "Tops out at 12 mph, below the Precor TRM 835 and Life Fitness Integrity",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The lowest-cost route to a commercial AC drive and the strongest residential warranty here. Confirm the seller and the circuit before you order.",
    description: "Spirit’s CT850 is a non-folding commercial treadmill sold for gyms and light-commercial rooms, and on Amazon it was the cheapest machine we found whose maker states an AC motor. Spirit’s product page, checked on 24 November 2026, gives a 4.0 HP brushless AC drive motor, a 0.3 mph startup speed, a speed range of 0.5 to 12 mph in 0.1 mph steps, an incline range of 0 to 15 in half steps, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, a 450 lb maximum user weight, set-up dimensions of 85 by 35.8 by 60.6 inches and an item weight of 390 lb. It lists a 120-volt NEMA 5-20P cord and recommends a 20-amp circuit; the owner’s manual we found describes a 15-amp dedicated circuit instead, so ask Spirit which applies. Spirit publishes two warranties: for US residential use, 10 years on the frame, lifetime on the motor and deck, 10 years on parts and two years on labour; for light-commercial use in facilities that do not charge dues, 10 years on the frame and five years on motor, deck and parts. The Amazon listing itself says little beyond commercial grade, a heavy-gauge steel frame and short lateral handrails, and its brand field shows Hydra Fitness Exchange, the seller, so check that you are buying a new unit with Spirit’s warranty. Amazon showed it at $2,083.89 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "life-fitness-integrity-clst",
    name: "Life Fitness Integrity Series CLST",
    brand: "Life Fitness",
    category: "Best AC treadmill for structured training and fitness tests",
    badge: "Most Programs",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00UGC5GCE?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41tk0Oi-OJL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/life-fitness-integrity-series-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "About $2,995 (Amazon, 24 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":2995,"high":2995},
    specs: "22 x 60 in. deck · 4 HP AC, 8 HP peak (Life Fitness) · 0.5–14 mph · up to 15% incline · 400 lb max user · dedicated 20A",
    pros: [
      "A 4 HP AC motor with an 8 HP peak rating, per Life Fitness",
      "0.5 to 14 mph in 0.1 mph steps, per Life Fitness",
      "Military and fitness-test programs including Army, Navy, Air Force and Marine tests, per the listing",
      "3.5-inch crowned steel rollers front and back, per the listing",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Life Fitness calls for a dedicated 20-amp circuit",
      "Life Fitness’s product page does not state the warranty",
      "The heaviest footprint to move here after the Precor TRM 885, at 425 lb",
    ],
    bottomLine: "A gym-standard club treadmill with the most structured programs here. Choose it if you train to tests or targets and can give it its own circuit.",
    description: "The Integrity Series is the treadmill many people know from hotel and health-club gyms, and the CLST is the version with the LED console. Life Fitness’s US product page, checked on 24 November 2026, gives a 4 hp AC motor with an 8.0 hp peak, a speed range of 0.5 to 14 mph in 0.1 mph steps, incline up to 15%, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, a 400 lb maximum user weight, dimensions of 82 by 36 by 56 inches, a unit weight of 425 lb, and a dedicated 20-amp, 120-volt circuit in the US. The Amazon listing adds the console detail: readouts including pace, watts, METs and distance climbed, an integrated reading rack, 3.5-inch precision crowned steel rollers and a long list of programs, among them Hill, Cardio, Fat Burn, heart-rate hill and interval workouts, 5K and 10K training, Army, Navy, Air Force and Marine fitness tests and six custom workouts. Life Fitness’s current page shows a newer console option, so check which console the seller is shipping. The product page does not state a warranty, so ask the seller for the written terms before you buy. Amazon showed it at $2,995.00 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "precor-trm-885",
    name: "Precor TRM 885",
    brand: "Precor",
    category: "Best AC treadmill with a touchscreen",
    badge: "Best Touchscreen",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00MFYDAL0?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41g0c-jBdgL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/precor-treadmills/",
    priceRange: "About $3,495 (Amazon, 24 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":3495,"high":3495},
    specs: "22 x 60 in. deck · 4 HP AC with PFC (Precor) · 400 lb max user · 120V/20A · touchscreen console",
    pros: [
      "A touchscreen console; Precor’s current page lists a 16-inch capacitive LCD (P84)",
      "The same 4 HP AC motor with power factor correction as the TRM 835, per Precor",
      "A 22 by 60-inch deck and 400 lb limit, per Precor",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The most expensive pick here, and the listing gives no bullets at all",
      "The listing title says P80 console; Precor now lists the P84, so confirm which you get",
      "Neither source states speed or incline range for this model",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For buyers who want the Precor 800-line build with a large screen. Check the console version and the seller first.",
    description: "The TRM 885 is the touchscreen model in Precor’s 800 line. The Amazon listing gives only its title, “Precor TRM 885 Treadmill with P80 Console”, with no feature bullets, so every figure here comes from Precor. Precor’s US product page, checked on 24 November 2026, lists a 4 HP AC drive motor with a power factor correction system, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, a 400 lb maximum user weight, a 120-volt, 20-amp supply in the US and Canada, dimensions of 83 by 35 by 68 inches and a weight of 430 lb. The current page describes the P84 console, a 16-inch capacitive LCD touchscreen, while the listing title names the earlier P80 console, so ask the seller which console is fitted and whether the unit is new. Neither the listing nor Precor’s page gave a speed or elevation range for this model, so we have not printed one. The case for it over the TRM 835 is the screen; the case against is the extra $700 or so and a thinner listing. Amazon showed it at $3,495.00 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "precor-trm-731",
    name: "Precor TRM 731",
    brand: "Precor",
    category: "Simplest AC treadmill to live with",
    badge: "Simplest Console",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B072M7RJ2Z?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41l7PPBbWOL._SL500_.jpg","width":418,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/precor-treadmills/",
    priceRange: "About $2,895 (Amazon, 24 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":2895,"high":2895},
    specs: "22 x 60 in. deck · 4 HP AC (Precor) · up to 12 mph · up to 15% incline · 400 lb max user · 120V/20A, NEMA 5-20R",
    pros: [
      "A 4 HP AC motor and 22 by 60-inch deck, per Precor",
      "Speeds up to 12 mph and up to 15% incline, per the listing",
      "A plain LED display with simple controls, per the listing",
      "The lightest Precor here at 405 lb, per Precor",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Costs more on Amazon than the more capable TRM 835 on the day we checked",
      "A short three-bullet listing; most figures come from Precor",
      "Needs a NEMA 5-20R receptacle on a 120-volt, 20-amp supply, per Precor",
    ],
    bottomLine: "A no-frills Precor AC treadmill. Worth it if the seller’s price drops below the TRM 835’s; otherwise the 835 does more for less.",
    description: "The TRM 731 is from Precor’s Experience line, a simpler commercial treadmill than the 800 series. The Amazon listing gives speeds up to 12 mph, incline up to 15%, an LED display with easy-to-use controls and Precor’s fit and gait technologies. Precor’s US product page, checked on 24 November 2026, adds a 4 HP AC drive motor, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, a 400 lb maximum user weight, a 120-volt, 20-amp supply with a NEMA 5-20R receptacle in the US and Canada, dimensions of 83 by 35 by 62 inches and a weight of 405 lb. That makes it the plainest machine here and the lightest of the three Precors. The odd thing on the day we checked was price: at $2,895.00 it cost more on Amazon than the TRM 835, which has a wider speed range and decline. Commercial treadmill prices on Amazon come from individual dealers and change often, so the 731 makes sense when its price falls below the 835’s, or for a buyer who wants the simplest possible console.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Best Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Best Treadmills With an AC Motor", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmills-with-ac-motor/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best treadmill with an AC motor?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On Amazon, the Precor TRM 835: a 4 HP AC motor, a 22 by 60-inch deck, 0.5 to 16 mph and -3% to 15% elevation, per Precor, for about $2,778 on 24 November 2026. Spirit’s CT850 is the value choice at about $2,084 with a 450 lb limit.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are AC motor treadmills better than DC?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For heavy, sustained commercial use, yes; for most homes, no. AC drives are built for long daily duty cycles, while DC motors are quieter at walking speeds, run from a normal outlet and cost far less. Our AC vs DC guide explains the trade-off in detail.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do I need a 20-amp outlet for an AC treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For the five machines here, plan on it. Precor lists 120 volts at 20 amps, Life Fitness calls for a dedicated 20-amp circuit for the Integrity, and Spirit recommends a 20-amp circuit for the CT850. Some AC models, such as Life Fitness’s Club Series+, are listed for a non-dedicated 120-volt supply, so check the specific model.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are there cheap AC motor treadmills on Amazon?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not that we could confirm. The cheapest maker-confirmed AC treadmill we found was the Spirit CT850 at about $2,084. Budget listings that put “AC” in the title often describe a permanent-magnet or brushless DC motor in their own bullets.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Sole make an AC motor treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The Sole TT8 is often described as one, and an older Sole spec sheet lists a 3.0 HP AC motor. Sole’s current product page lists only “4.0 HP” without saying AC or DC, and showed the TT8 as sold out on 24 November 2026, so we left it off this list.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you fold a commercial AC treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "None of the five on this page folds, and commercial AC treadmills very rarely do. They weigh 390 to 430 lb assembled, per their makers, and are meant to stay in one place. If you need to fold the treadmill, choose a home model with a strong DC motor.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-24",
      dateModified: "2026-11-24",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              ...(product.amazonUrl ? { url: product.amazonUrl } : {}),
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 5,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmills-with-ac-motor/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-treadmills-with-ac-motor/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "best");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-24",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-24",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "ac motor treadmill",
      "treadmill with ac motor",
      "best ac motor treadmill",
      "commercial treadmill ac motor",
      "ac treadmill for home",
      "commercial grade treadmill for home",
      "treadmill 20 amp circuit",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: Precor TRM 835", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Treadmills With an AC Motor Commercial-Grade Picks</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        The best treadmill with an AC motor you can buy on Amazon is the Precor TRM 835: a 4 HP AC drive, a 22 by 60-inch deck, 0.5 to 16 mph and -3% to 15% elevation for about $2,778. Spirit’s CT850 is the value pick at about $2,084 with a 450 lb limit, and every machine here is a commercial treadmill that expects a 20-amp circuit.
      </p>
      <p class="ed-answer"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best Overall: <a href="#precor-trm-835">Precor TRM 835</a>. Best Value: <a href="#spirit-ct850">Spirit Fitness CT850</a>. Most Programs: <a href="#life-fitness-integrity-clst">Life Fitness Integrity Series CLST</a>.</p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 24, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">How we chose: makers’ published specifications and manuals, independent reviews and owner reports, cross-checked. Not tested hands-on.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We may earn a commission when you buy through the links below. It costs you nothing and never decides a ranking. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#precor-trm-835"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41eY1JIjdGL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Precor TRM 835" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#spirit-ct850"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31AUwG1hAwL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Spirit Fitness CT850" width="333" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#life-fitness-integrity-clst"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41tk0Oi-OJL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Life Fitness Integrity Series CLST" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Precor TRM 835 · Spirit Fitness CT850 · Life Fitness Integrity Series CLST</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Almost every treadmill sold for home use runs on a DC motor, and that is the right choice for
          most homes. AC drive motors belong to the commercial world: gym treadmills that run twelve or
          more hours a day, take heavy users back to back and are expected to last a decade. Amazon sells
          very few of them, and the ones it does sell are listed by commercial brands with thin
          listings, high round-number prices and, often, a third-party seller. The five treadmills
          below are the AC-motor machines we could find on Amazon US on 24 November 2026 whose maker
          states an AC motor on its own product page or brochure. We read each listing, checked each
          maker page, and left out machines where we could not confirm the motor type.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Overall:</span> <a href="#precor-trm-835">Precor TRM 835</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Value:</span> <a href="#spirit-ct850">Spirit Fitness CT850</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Programs:</span> <a href="#life-fitness-integrity-clst">Life Fitness Integrity Series CLST</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Touchscreen:</span> <a href="#precor-trm-885">Precor TRM 885</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Simplest Console:</span> <a href="#precor-trm-731">Precor TRM 731</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this roundup">
          <h2>In this roundup</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#quick-picks">The short answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#picks">The 5 picks</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-we-chose">How We Chose These Treadmills</a></li>
            <li><a href="#why-ac">Why AC</a></li>
            <li><a href="#power-and-wiring">Power and wiring</a></li>
            <li><a href="#space-and-delivery">Space and delivery</a></li>
            <li><a href="#sellers-and-warranty">Sellers and warranty</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reading-listings">Reading listings</a></li>
            <li><a href="#when-not-to-buy">When to skip AC</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="quick-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Best Treadmill With an AC Motor: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Buy the Precor TRM 835 if you want the most capable AC treadmill on Amazon; buy the
            Spirit CT850 if you want an AC motor for the least money and the highest weight limit; buy the
            Life Fitness Integrity Series CLST if you want a club treadmill with a long list of built-in
            fitness tests.</strong> The <a href="/precor-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Precor TRM</a> 885 is the 835’s touchscreen sibling, and the Precor
            TRM 731 is the plainest of the five, with an LED console and a 12 mph top speed.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Price band:</strong> about $2,084 to $3,495 on Amazon on 24 November 2026.</li>
            <li><strong>Motor:</strong> 4 HP AC on all five, per Precor, <a href="/life-fitness/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Life Fitness</a> and Spirit.</li>
