        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What is the best treadmill with an AC motor?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Amazon, the Precor TRM 835: a 4 HP AC motor, a 22 by 60-inch deck, 0.5 to 16 mph and -3% to 15% elevation, per Precor, for about $2,778 on 24 November 2026. Spirit’s CT850 is the value choice at about $2,084 with a 450 lb limit.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are AC motor treadmills better than DC?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For heavy, sustained commercial use, yes; for most homes, no. AC drives are built for long daily duty cycles, while DC motors are quieter at walking speeds, run from a normal outlet and cost far less. Our AC vs DC guide explains the trade-off in detail.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do I need a 20-amp outlet for an AC treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For the five machines here, plan on it. Precor lists 120 volts at 20 amps, Life Fitness calls for a dedicated 20-amp circuit for the Integrity, and Spirit recommends a 20-amp circuit for the CT850. Some AC models, such as Life Fitness’s Club Series+, are listed for a non-dedicated 120-volt supply, so check the specific model.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are there cheap AC motor treadmills on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not that we could confirm. The cheapest maker-confirmed AC treadmill we found was the Spirit CT850 at about $2,084. Budget listings that put “AC” in the title often describe a permanent-magnet or brushless DC motor in their own bullets.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Sole make an AC motor treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The Sole TT8 is often described as one, and an older Sole spec sheet lists a 3.0 HP AC motor. Sole’s current product page lists only “4.0 HP” without saying AC or DC, and showed the TT8 as sold out on 24 November 2026, so we left it off this list.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you fold a commercial AC treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              None of the five on this page folds, and commercial AC treadmills very rarely do. They weigh 390 to 430 lb assembled, per their makers, and are meant to stay in one place. If you need to fold the treadmill, choose a home model with a strong DC motor.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

